         0.15.1 (.github#1718) — MAKE `scripts/skill-view`'S OWN SOURCES FOLLOWABLE. PATCH.
         0.15.0 shipped `scripts/skill-view` with two RELATIVE `# shellcheck source=lib/...` pragmas
         and no file-scoped `# shellcheck source-path=SCRIPTDIR`, so shellcheck resolved them against
         its own working directory rather than the script's and linted the file with BOTH libraries
         unread — SC1091 twice, from the repository root, which is how every gate in this org invokes
         it. This adds the one directive, above the first command, where it is file-scoped.
         PATCH, and each clause of that is checkable. The MEMBER SET IS UNCHANGED (28), every
         destination and mode is unchanged, no materialize property is added or altered, and
         `skill-view`'s RUNTIME BEHAVIOUR is identical — the only bytes that move are a comment
         block in one `kind: client` member. Nothing a 0.15.0 reader was told is now false, and no
         receiver has to do anything differently. It is the same class as 0.8.1 (edc8404).
         WHY IT COULD NOT BE FIXED IN THE RECEIVER, which is what makes this a kit release rather
         than seven one-line PRs: `scripts/skill-view` is a kit-materialized file, so a directive
         written into a receiver's tree is reverted by its next FsggKitMaterialize and reds
         `coordination-sync` in its against-pin check mode in the meantime. FS.GG.Game found it, and
         the reason only it could is that its shell
         gate is the only one in the org that runs at `-S info` and treats an unfollowed `source` as
         a red in its own right — and its 0.15.0 bump (Game#514, run 30321396512) was red on this and
